-- title:
--   One level of the cocycle-twisted p-divisible tower
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$, the ideal $(p)$ is maximal and $\mathcal O$ is $(p)$-adically complete; let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional commutative formal group law over $\mathcal O$ (a $d$-tuple of power series in $2d$ variables with vanishing constant term, linear terms the two identity matrices, satisfying associativity and, by `IsComm`, symmetry), and let $h$ be such that the reduction of the iterate series $[p]_\Phi$ modulo $(p)$ cuts out a quotient of $(\mathcal O/p)[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ of dimension $p^h$ over $\mathcal O/p$. Let $E$ be a commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra, finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module, and let $v$ be such that the $p^v$-th convolution power of $\mathrm{id}_E$ equals the counit followed by the unit (so $E$ is killed by $p^v$). Let $c_2 : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to E\otimes_{\mathcal O}E$ have all components in $(p)$, and assume, for every commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $g$ in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor and which is $(p)$-adically complete: normalisation (for each $\mathcal O$-algebra map $f : E \to g$, the two evaluations of $c_2$ in which one factor is $f$ and the other the composite of the counit with the unit vanish), symmetry (the two evaluations at $(f,f')$ and $(f',f)$ agree), and the $\Phi$-cocycle identity: for all $f,f',f''$, $c_2(f,f') +_\Phi c_2(f\ast f',f'') = c_2(f',f'') +_\Phi c_2(f, f'\ast f'')$, where $\ast$ denotes the convolution of two $\mathcal O$-algebra maps through the comultiplication of $E$ and $+_\Phi$ is $p$-adic evaluation of $\Phi$ at the relevant points. Let $C : \mathbb N \to \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to E$ be the associated power defects: $C_0 = 0$, $C_{n+1} = C_n +_\Phi m\bigl(([n]\otimes \mathrm{id})(c_2)\bigr)$ with $m$ the multiplication of $E$ and $[n]$ the $n$-th convolution power of $\mathrm{id}_E$, each $C_n$ has components in $(p)$ and counit $0$, and the product formula $\Delta(C_n) +_\Phi [n]_\Phi(c_2) = (C_n\otimes 1) +_\Phi \bigl((1\otimes C_n) +_\Phi ([n]\otimes[n])(c_2)\bigr)$ holds in $E\otimes_{\mathcal O}E$. Then there exist a commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra $L_v$, finite and free over $\mathcal O$, a bialgebra map $\iota : E \to L_v$, and $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\Psi : \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] \to L_v$ and $\theta : E[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] \to L_v$ such that: $\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal O} L_v = p^{vh}\,\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal O} E$; $\theta$ is surjective, sends the constant $e$ to $\iota(e)$ and $X_i$ to $\Psi(X_i)$, and $\ker\theta$ is generated by the $d$ elements obtained from the $i$-th component of $[p^v]_\Phi$ (coefficients pushed into $E$) by subtracting the constant series with value the $i$-th coordinate of the formal inverse series of $\Phi$ evaluated $p$-adically at $C_{p^v}$; each $\Psi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)$ in $L_v$, $\Psi$ is given on all of $\mathcal O[[X]]$ by $p$-adic evaluation at the points $\Psi(X_i)$, the counit kills each $\Psi(X_i)$, each $\Psi([p^v]_\Phi{}_i)$ lies in $(p)$, and the algebra map $E\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal O[[X]] \to L_v$ determined by $\iota$ and $\Psi$ is surjective; finally the comultiplication satisfies $\Delta(\Psi X_i) = \bigl((\Psi X\otimes 1) +_\Phi \bigl((1\otimes \Psi X) +_\Phi (\iota\otimes\iota)(c_2)\bigr)\bigr)_i$ in $L_v\otimes_{\mathcal O}L_v$, and for every $n$ the $n$-th convolution power of $\mathrm{id}_{L_v}$ sends $\Psi(X_i)$ to $\bigl([n]_\Phi(\Psi X) +_\Phi \iota(C_n)\bigr)_i$, all $\Phi$-sums being computed by $p$-adic evaluation.
--
--   This constructs a single level of the $p$-divisible tower attached to a symmetric normalised $2$-cocycle $c_2$ twisting the formal group $\Phi$ by the finite Hopf algebra $E$: the level algebra $L_v$ is presented as $E[[X]]$ modulo $[p^v]_\Phi(X)$ shifted by the power defect $C_{p^v}$, with comultiplication and convolution powers given by $\Phi$-addition twisted by $c_2$. It is used by [`MvFormalGroup.exists_pDivisibleTower_of_cocycle`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_pDivisibleTower_of_cocycle), which assembles these levels, with their transition maps, into a $p$-divisible group over $\mathcal O$.
